.TH RSA2SSHTEST 1
.SH NAME
rsa2sshtest \- regression test for rsa2ssh(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rsa2sshtest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Rsa2sshtest
loads
.BR /dis/auth/rsa2ssh.dis 's
in-process test seam,
.BR run(argv,\ keyline) ,
and checks it against a real, live oracle: plan9port's own
.B rsa2ssh
binary (this host's only installed copy), run through
.IR emu 's
host-command-execution device
.RB ( #C ,
see
.IR cmd (3)).
.PP
The oracle needs
.B -2
to get the
.B ssh-rsa
-format output this file translates - unpatched, plan9port's own copy
still defaults to an older plain-decimal format 9front's own
.B rsa2ssh.c
dropped entirely; confirmed directly against the binary before writing
this test, not assumed (see
.IR rsa2ssh (1)'s
own SOURCE entry).
.PP
Test keys are real RSA moduli (from
.B "openssl genrsa"
and
.BR ssh-keygen ),
cross-checked field-by-field against
.BR "openssl rsa -text" 's
own independent decoding before use here - not placeholder hex.
.SH SOURCE
.B appl/cmd/auth/rsa2sshtest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR rsa2ssh (1)
.SH BUGS
Does not exercise the
.I file
command-line-argument path (every case here drives
.BR run() 's
own
.I keyline
string directly).
